  "output_text": "- **Continuation is teacher-forced, not resampled:** the baseline run generates `max_new_tokens` once; each recompute feeds `prompt + ids[:step]` and asks for exactly one new token, so the compared next-token distribution is conditioned on the same committed prefix rather than on an independently sampled trajectory.\n\n- **Cache boundaries are the listed prefix lengths:** `--prefix-lengths` defaults to `68,69,70,127,128,129,255,256,257`, i.e. it probes just below, at, and just above power-of-two-ish block boundaries; each length is converted to `step = length - len(prompt)` and must fall inside the baseline completion.\n\n- **Numerical differences reported are top-logprob diagnostics, not bitwise parity:** `compare` reports top-1 equality, cached vs. recompute top-1 margins, top-`n` overlap ratio",
